  "caption": "Quinn opened a salon, Quinn's Cuts, and spent eight hours a day with arms up and head tilted. By 5pm: neck, shoulders and a headache. The dentist next door felt the same.\n\nWhen the arms are held up without support, neck and shoulder muscles keep working, and fatigue builds over the day, especially in the same position on the same side.\n\nTips that can help: rest your forearms when you can, bring the work closer, take 30-second micro-breaks, switch sides and mix up tasks, and build neck and shoulder endurance. Lighter, sharper tools may reduce grip effort too.\n\nNight-time hand numbness, weakness or worsening pain is worth getting checked. Daily headaches warrant a chat with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
